### Variables — VS Code REST Client (humao.rest-client)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = test@example.com
@password = password123

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Register a new user
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Tokens captured from the login response
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.access_token}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.refresh_token}}

### Current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Refresh tokens (rotates the refresh token — old one becomes invalid)
# @name refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Logout (revokes the refresh token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Ingest a document
# @name ingest
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Rust Facts",
  "content": "Rust is a systems programming language that guarantees memory safety without a garbage collector, using an ownership system with borrowing and lifetimes.\n\nThe Rust compiler is called rustc, and the package manager is called Cargo. Packages in Rust are called crates and are published to crates.io.\n\nRust was originally created by Graydon Hoare at Mozilla Research, with the first stable release, Rust 1.0, shipping in May 2015."
}

### List documents
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Delete a document
@documentId = {{ingest.response.body.id}}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### RAG chat — ask a question about your documents
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Who created Rust and when was 1.0 released?"
}

### RAG chat with custom top_k
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "What is the Rust package manager called?",
  "top_k": 3
}
